## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical implementation of privacy safeguards in Azure OpenAI within multi-tenant SaaS, focusing on data leakage prevention, RBAC, and auditable logging.

## Key Concepts
- PII detection and redaction pipelines
- Grounding with Cognitive Search over a versioned KB
- Per-tenant RBAC with Azure AD
- Data Lake auditing
- GDPR/CCPA compliance checks and synthetic-data tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: redaction before OpenAI call
async function process(input, tenantId) {
  const pii = detectPII(input);
  const redacted = redact(input, pii);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(redacted, tenantId);
  return await openai.complete(prompt);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify no PII leaks in logs or prompts across tenants?
- What metrics ensure latency remains acceptable under load?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design policy-grounded assistants with explainable outputs and integrated escalation.

## Key Concepts
- Grounding with Cognitive Search embeddings
- Confidence scoring and provenance tracking
- Safe escalation to ticketing (ServiceNow)
- Data lineage and logging for audits

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: compute final answer with grounding and provenance
async function answer(query) {
  const docs = await searchKB(query);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(query, docs);
  const res = await openai.complete({ prompt });
  const provenance = docs.map(d => d.id);
  const confidence = res.meta?.confidence ?? 0.9;
  if (confidence < 0.8) await ticketSystem.create('Review needed', { query, provenance });
  return { text: res.text, confidence, provenance };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle KB versioning and rollback?
- How would you validate calibration of confidence scores in production?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a practical, beginner-friendly multi-tenant flow with prompt catalog versioning, failover, and privacy controls in Azure OpenAI.

## Key Concepts

- API Management routing with tenant context
- Versioned prompt catalog stored in Azure Blob
- Per-tenant quotas and graceful fallback
- PII redaction via Text Analytics before OpenAI calls
- Regional OpenAI endpoints and observability

## Code Example

```javascript
async function routeRequest(tenantId, payload) {
  const tmpl = await blob.get(`prompts/${tenantId}/v1.json`);
  const redacted = pii.redact(payload.prompt, payload.user);
  const finalPrompt = `${tmpl.promptPrefix}\n${redacted}`;
  return openai.chat(finalPrompt);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test failover if the catalog fetch fails?
- How would you monitor per-tenant quotas and trigger alerts?

